Root cause:
The bug was caused by the attempt to access a field in the `chip_info` structure that was intended to be constant, but was being modified in the `rtw8821c_phy_set_param` function. This led to a core dump due to a page fault when the code tried to write to a read-only memory location. The solution involved moving the `ch_param` field to a different structure (`rtw_hal`) that allows for both reading and writing, thus preventing the illegal memory access.
